:answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352199} {:answer/id #uuid "82f2ca61-6f60-55c4-b394-f386a4ef3a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352710} {:answer/id #uuid "bdecff94-cfcf-519e-9706-a0631fc4bc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353189} {:answer/id #uuid "d49e801a-dd10-5fa8-a701-1683b101139d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdecff94-cfcf-519e-9706-a0631fc4bc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353189} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d9eb463-feb6-54fd-8e37-433447a4c980" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29047b99-0717-54ea-8401-af32e706bd20" :question/math-academy-id "q-84982" :question/problem "Victoria has the $4$ playing cards: the ace of clubs, the ace of diamonds, the ace of hearts, and the ace of spades. She takes one card and places it in front of her. She then does the same with another card. In how many different ways can she choose a sequence of $2$ cards like this?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $4$ cards, so $n=4.$ We want to select $2$ of those cards to make a sequence of $2$ cards, so we have $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to choose the cards is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{4}{P}_{2} & =\\frac{4!}{(4-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4!}{2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{\\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "256d3a08-0ade-51e9-887b-67250d5fae21" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Permutations of Objects Chosen From a Group of at Least Ten"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4519364a-a039-5b52-8828-103d442a03a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "990" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418408} {:answer/id #uuid "5456ddc8-8ae6-57cd-97e3-f1eaa26ffc00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,400" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418409} {:answer/id #uuid "862c4b09-9172-545f-97c9-7f21e79cd3de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,980" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418410} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a2ab60-18b2-5943-9f8e-856a28f1c403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55\\,440" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418411} {:answer/id #uuid "ea315232-2913-5a30-877a-c82272b5ac01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,920" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea315232-2913-5a30-877a-c82272b5ac01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,920" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418412} :answer-field/id #uuid "69ac052e-a374-5b6c-af86-f7bda6ec7c19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a0bfa46-736f-571e-9fd1-af2e7c4186b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-84984" :question/problem "A soccer coach must choose a defensive lineup for each of the $4$ defensive positions from a roster of $11$ defenders. How many potential starting defensive lineups are there?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $11$ defenders, so $n=11.$ We want to select $4$ of those defenders to play in each of the $4$ positions, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different starting defensive lineups is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{11}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{11!}{(11-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11!}{7!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot \\cancel{7!}}{\\cancel{7!}} \\\\  & =11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =7\\,920.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
